  "limits": [
    "The full run includes all effect-slot logic and the original kernel artifact workflow. Later error-registry additions, export verifier and artifact fsync changes are covered by focused tests, a final executable run, and all-target Clippy.",
    "The final fault run strengthens process evidence with SIGKILL signal assertions and a shared eight-process start barrier.",
    "Fault subprocesses directly exercise the store/effect boundary. They do not instantiate the entire kernel recovery pipeline.",
    "The artifact demonstration uses two in-process kernels and static native policy proposals. It is not a remote deployment or live model workload.",
    "Receipt databases are left in the temporary run directory. The retained export includes signed receipts, outcome, result, artifact bytes, and a read-only receiver-slot snapshot.",
    "Offline verification validates specified bindings and recomputes the scope contract. It does not prove global non-duplication.",
    "An equally stateful baseline and end-to-end multi-receiver crash recovery remain unimplemented."
  ]
